    "detailed_description": "<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Awake, arise or be for ever fall\u2019n.</h2><i>Waking with no memory on a strange planet.<br><br>Your journey for answers and choices made<br>will shape the course of history.</i><br><br><strong>Fall from Space</strong> is a non-linear\u200b open world RPG for the Gameboy,<br>with an epic story spanning a solar system.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Features</h2><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li>Jet off to the stars! Multiple worlds to \u200bexplore inside your Gameboy, with side quests, unique encounters, secrets and upgrades<br></li><li>\u200bCombines Metroidvanian action with an open world RPG<br></li><li>An original story to uncover with multiple endings, a karma system and choices that impact the world and it's inhabitants around you<br></li><li>Authentic Gameboy aesthetic, with graphics and art style built within the DMG palette constraints<br></li><li>Hours of gameplay, save at any time with multiple save slots<br></li><li>Designed and developed by a Solo Developer to run on actual Gameboy (and Analogue Pocket) hardware, with a Steam (Win/Mac/Linux) port<br></li><li>Original Soundtrack, scored by Beatscribe</li></ul><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Background</h2><br>Inspired by Paradise Lost and 90s CRPGs such as Fallout 2, Planescape and Buck Rogers Countdown to Doomsday, it's an ARPG with plenty of retro platforming action, a player karma system, side quests, multiple endings, a brand new soundtrack (coming soon) and large non-linear maps filled with secrets.<br><br>Download the Alpha demo now to explore the South of the first planet, (full demo coming to Steam soon) and follow for progress updates (and I'd love any feedback), <br><br>Note: This isn't a Gameboy style game, it's an original game developed within the limitations of and designed to run on original hardware and the Analogue Pocket.",
    "about_the_game": "<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Awake, arise or be for ever fall\u2019n.</h2><i>Waking with no memory on a strange planet.<br><br>Your journey for answers and choices made<br>will shape the course of history.</i><br><br><strong>Fall from Space</strong> is a non-linear\u200b open world RPG for the Gameboy,<br>with an epic story spanning a solar system.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Features</h2><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li>Jet off to the stars! Multiple worlds to \u200bexplore inside your Gameboy, with side quests, unique encounters, secrets and upgrades<br></li><li>\u200bCombines Metroidvanian action with an open world RPG<br></li><li>An original story to uncover with multiple endings, a karma system and choices that impact the world and it's inhabitants around you<br></li><li>Authentic Gameboy aesthetic, with graphics and art style built within the DMG palette constraints<br></li><li>Hours of gameplay, save at any time with multiple save slots<br></li><li>Designed and developed by a Solo Developer to run on actual Gameboy (and Analogue Pocket) hardware, with a Steam (Win/Mac/Linux) port<br></li><li>Original Soundtrack, scored by Beatscribe</li></ul><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Background</h2><br>Inspired by Paradise Lost and 90s CRPGs such as Fallout 2, Planescape and Buck Rogers Countdown to Doomsday, it's an ARPG with plenty of retro platforming action, a player karma system, side quests, multiple endings, a brand new soundtrack (coming soon) and large non-linear maps filled with secrets.<br><br>Download the Alpha demo now to explore the South of the first planet, (full demo coming to Steam soon) and follow for progress updates (and I'd love any feedback), <br><br>Note: This isn't a Gameboy style game, it's an original game developed within the limitations of and designed to run on original hardware and the Analogue Pocket.",
    "short_description": "Fall from Space is a non-linear, sci-fi ARPG for the Gameboy. Combining Metroidvanian action with an open world RPG, and an epic story that spans a solar system.",
